Good morning everyone,

With budget season wrapping up, here are the travel and expense rates that will apply from January 1, 2025, under version 3.2 of the Travel and Expense Policy.

  * Meals and incidentals per diem: $55 per full travel day ($70 in Port Averill, Hollins Bay and Dunmere). First and last day at 75%.
  * Hotel caps: $195 per night, $270 in the high-cost cities.
  * Mileage: 60 cents per mile.
  * Receipts: required for any expense of $25 or more.
  * Expense reports: please submit within 60 days of your trip.
  * Approvals: your manager can approve reports up to $750. Above that, your department head also approves, and reports over $2,500 go to the CFO as well.

Clearline will be updated over the holiday week, so reports for trips in December 2024 will use the 2024 rates even if you submit them in January.

If you have questions, reply to this email or call extension 4410.

Thanks, and happy early holidays,

Tobiah Grant
Finance Operations Manager
Calloway Ridge Credit Union
